From: K2B_RetroArch
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: kickpi-k2b: hold the PHY out of reset from early boot

The K2B V2.2's MAE0621A must answer its ID read for its driver (0062) to
bind, and that driver is what starts the RGMII RX clock the EMAC reset
needs. With PI6 as the PHY node's reset-gpios it is still low at the ID
read (our U-Boot has networking off and leaves it low). As the MDIO bus's
reset-gpios it is pulsed and the scan runs 100 ms later, and the PHY does
not answer that soon either. Both ended in "EMAC reset timeout".
Hog PI6 high instead, from pin controller registration on, and never
pulse it. Verified on the board: with the PHY long out of reset, ID
0x7b744411, MAE0621A-Q2C bound, link 1 Gbps.

---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h618-kickpi-k2b.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h618-kickpi-k2b.dts
@@ -199,12 +199,29 @@
 };
 
 &mdio0 {
+	/* No reset-gpios: PI6 is hogged high below. K2B_RetroArch 0064. */
 	ext_rgmii_phy: ethernet-phy@0 {
 		compatible = "ethernet-phy-ieee802.3-c22";
 		reg = <0x0>;
-		reset-assert-us = <20000>;
-		reset-deassert-us = <100000>;
-		reset-gpios = <&pio 8 6 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>; /* PI6 */
+	};
+};
+
+&pio {
+	/*
+	 * PI6 is the MAE0621A's nRESET. Keep it released from the moment the
+	 * pin controller registers, about 0.8 s before the EMAC probes, and
+	 * never pulse it. The PHY must answer its ID read for its driver
+	 * (0062) to bind, and that driver starts the RGMII RX clock the EMAC
+	 * reset needs. Measured on the board: 100 ms after a reset pulse the
+	 * ID read still fails (PHY-node and bus-level reset-gpios both ended
+	 * in "EMAC reset timeout"); with the PHY long out of reset it reads
+	 * 0x7b744411 and the link comes up at 1 Gbps.
+	 */
+	emac0-phy-nreset-hog {
+		gpio-hog;
+		gpios = <8 6 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
+		output-high;
+		line-name = "emac0-phy-nreset";
 	};
 };
 
